From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Burker <burker@ucs.at>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: context: honour IPV6_PKTINFO interface on send

Zephyr takes the source address of a UDP datagram from the IPV6_PKTINFO
ancillary data of a send call (get_msg_src_addr_hint()), but ignores its
outgoing interface index (ipi6_ifindex), so an application cannot pin the
egress interface of the datagram.

Add a helper that returns the IPV6_PKTINFO carried by a send call and select
the egress interface from its ipi6_ifindex in context_sendto(), ahead of the
destination-based selection and only when the interface was not already chosen
by the multicast or link-local logic. As the interface is set on the context
before the packet is allocated, the source address hint is then checked against
that interface.

The change is inert when no IPV6_PKTINFO send cmsg is present or its
ipi6_ifindex is 0. This mirrors the IPV6_PKTINFO send behaviour of Linux and BSD
sockets and lets the KNX-IoT Wi-Fi port reply, on multi-interface boards (e.g.
Ethernet plus Wi-Fi), on the interface a request arrived on.
---
 subsys/net/ip/net_context.c | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subsys/net/ip/net_context.c b/subsys/net/ip/net_context.c
index fb7080cc92..a619726bec 100644
--- a/subsys/net/ip/net_context.c
+++ b/subsys/net/ip/net_context.c
@@ -2430,6 +2430,32 @@ static bool get_msg_src_addr_hint(const struct net_msghdr *msg, net_sa_family_t
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* Return the IPV6_PKTINFO ancillary data supplied by the application on a send
+ * call, or NULL when none is present. Zephyr already takes the source address
+ * from it (get_msg_src_addr_hint()); this is for the outgoing interface index
+ * (ipi6_ifindex), which context_sendto() uses to pick the egress interface, as
+ * Linux and BSD sockets do.
+ */
+static const struct net_in6_pktinfo *get_tx_pktinfo6(const struct net_msghdr *msg)
+{
+	struct net_cmsghdr *cmsg;
+
+	if (msg == NULL || msg->msg_control == NULL || msg->msg_controllen == 0) {
+		return NULL;
+	}
+
+	for (cmsg = NET_CMSG_FIRSTHDR(msg); cmsg != NULL;
+	     cmsg = NET_CMSG_NXTHDR(msg, cmsg)) {
+		if (cmsg->cmsg_len == NET_CMSG_LEN(sizeof(struct net_in6_pktinfo)) &&
+		    cmsg->cmsg_level == NET_IPPROTO_IPV6 &&
+		    cmsg->cmsg_type == ZSOCK_IPV6_PKTINFO) {
+			return (struct net_in6_pktinfo *)NET_CMSG_DATA(cmsg);
+		}
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 static int context_setup_udp_packet(struct net_context *context,
 				    net_sa_family_t family,
 				    struct net_pkt *pkt,
@@ -3017,6 +3043,22 @@ static int context_sendto(struct net_context *context,
 			}
 		}
 
+		/* An explicit outgoing interface supplied through IPV6_PKTINFO takes
+		 * precedence over the destination-based interface selection below. This
+		 * is required on multi-interface boards (e.g. Ethernet plus Wi-Fi) so a
+		 * reply leaves on the interface the request arrived on.
+		 */
+		if (iface == NULL && msghdr != NULL) {
+			const struct net_in6_pktinfo *pktinfo = get_tx_pktinfo6(msghdr);
+
+			if (pktinfo != NULL && pktinfo->ipi6_ifindex > 0) {
+				iface = net_if_get_by_index(pktinfo->ipi6_ifindex);
+				if (iface != NULL) {
+					net_context_set_iface(context, iface);
+				}
+			}
+		}
+
 		/* If application has not yet set the destination address
 		 * i.e., by not calling connect(), then set the interface
 		 * here so that the packet gets sent to the correct network
-- 
